<%# The footer's report popup — the ONE place an operator reports a problem,
    what they expected, or a suggestion.

    It is a POPUP rather than a page for the same reason the engine light
    lives in the footer: an operator reports a problem from wherever
    they hit it, and navigating away to a form would take them off the page they
    are describing. The page, the account and the version are captured by the
    controller from the request, so being on the page IS the context.

    The standard popup shape (.popup > .popup-panel > .popup-head + .popup-body)
    with the app's ONE close mechanism, because openPopup/closePopup in
    aether.js look for exactly these. The trigger is `data-popup` on the footer
    button, handled by the same delegated listener as every other popup — so this
    is wiring, not a second mechanism.

    `hidden` is what keeps it shut, and it is the FIRST thing openPopup clears;
    the [hidden] { display: none !important } rule is what makes that reliable. %>
<div class="popup" id="bug-report-popup" role="dialog" aria-modal="true"
     aria-labelledby="bug-report-popup-title" hidden>
  <div class="popup-panel popup-report">
    <header class="popup-head">
      <h2 id="bug-report-popup-title">
        <%= image_tag "maint-worker-32.png", alt: "", class: "report-head-icon" %>
        Report a problem
      </h2>
      <button type="button" class="popup-close" data-popup-close aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    </header>
    <div class="popup-body">
      <p class="jev-question">
        What went wrong, what you expected instead, or anything you would change.
        It goes to the project's issue tracker for triage, with this page and your
        account attached.
      </p>
      <%= render "bug_reports/form" %>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
